cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, dataset, or trained models, please cite as follows."
type: software
title: "Guzheng music generation: fine-tuning NotaGen for traditional Chinese music"
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Anjie"
    email: "anjiehst@gmail.com"
abstract: >
  Code, dataset, and trained models for generating traditional Chinese guzheng music
  using hierarchical patch-character language models. Compares a fine-tune of
  NotaGen-medium (pre-trained on ~1M Western scores) against an identical-architecture
  model trained from scratch on the same corpus, isolating the contribution of
  pre-training. Includes 26 hand-curated guzheng repertoire pieces, 99 pieces from
  the Guzheng-Tech99 dataset, and 1,875 ABC samples (125 pieces × 15 keys).
keywords:
  - music-generation
  - guzheng
  - chinese-music
  - abc-notation
  - language-models
  - notagen
